        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Keogh Auctioneers are delighted to present 2 Copperalley Close, Greencloyne, Youghal, Co. Cork, P36 C638 for sale by private treaty.\n\nNumber 2 Copperalley Close is a magnificent detached two-storey home superbly located in one of Youghal's most sought-after addresses.\n\nCopperalley Close itself is an exclusive enclave of just 30 individually designed detached homes located in a suburban area on the northern approach to Youghal town. It offers easy access to the N25 CorkWaterford Road, with the town centre and supermarkets within walking distance and Youghal's three Blue Flag beaches only a short drive away.\n\nNumber 2 sits at the entrance to the enclave and benefits from a lovely view over Copperalley GAA Playing Fields and Mistletoe Castle beyond.\n\nBuilt in 2000, this beautifully designed high-end property offers luxurious contemporary living in a very private setting.\n\nThe house has achieved a B energy rating, thanks to energy-efficient features including triple-glazed windows throughout and underfloor heating in the kitchen and dining room.\n\nOn arrival, the property makes an immediate impression with its attractive façade and welcoming exterior. A walled and gated driveway provides ample off-street parking, while the front landscaped grounds feature mature trees, kerbed lawns, raised beds and established planting.\n\nA tiled entrance porch with a stylish green front door is cleverly positioned to the side of the house and opens into an elegant reception hall with timber flooring.\n\nThe ground floor includes two beautifully styled reception rooms. One is arranged as a library, with dual-aspect bay windows, bespoke “Waterford Wood” fitted carpentry and a feature open fireplace. The second has a contemporary design in muted blue tones and opens onto a fabulous south-facing conservatory.\n\nThe fully fitted kitchen has a modern high end finish and includes a gorgeous lounge area with a stove, a lovely place to relax while keeping an eye on the cooking. Sliding doors lead from the kitchen into the dining room, which, like the library, features bespoke “Waterford Wood” fitted carpentry. The room also enjoys sweeping views across the playing pitch towards Mistletoe Castle and West Waterford.\n\nA utility room and guest WC complete the ground floor accommodation.\n\nA timber staircase with a bespoke decorative wrought-iron banisters leads to the first floor, where the accommodation includes four beautifully appointed bedrooms and a family bathroom. The principal bedroom is spacious and stylish, complete with a gorgeous ensuite. One bedroom is currently arranged as a dressing room. The remaining bedrooms are generous doubles and one also includes an ensuite shower room. Each bedroom features fitted Sliderobe wardrobes.\n\nThe south-facing rear garden is exceptionally private and a true highlight of the property.\n\nCurrently arranged as a spacious patio area, it features contemporary raised beds, established planting, and a striking red-brick wall with a timber door that gives the space a Mediterranean feel. Steps from the patio lead to a beautiful raised terraced lawn area with a garden shed.\n\nNumber 2 Copperalley Close is an exceptionally attractive and enviable home, offering discerning buyers the chance to acquire a beautifully presented, move-in-ready property in a superb location.\n\nDream homes of this calibre rarely come to market, and viewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate all that this exceptional property has to offer.\n\nTitle: Freehold"
